/build
/build-asan
# The fuzzing build, and everything afl-fuzz writes beneath it: the queue it
# grows, the crashes it saves, its statistics. All of it is produced, some of
# it runs to thousands of files, and none of it is source.
/build-fuzz
# What the demo writes beside itself when it is asked for a screenshot. It was
# committed once, 5.6 MB of raw pixels that nothing builds and nothing reads.
/schultz_demo.ppm
/.idea

# third_party is source only, and all of it is committed: the upstream
# archives in third_party/src plus the vendored test framework. Nothing there
# is generated, so nothing there is ignored.
#
# Everything a dependency build produces goes under build-deps/<target>/
# instead: extracted sources, build trees, and the install prefix. One
# checkout can hold several targets at once and none of them is in git.
/build-deps

# docs/api is generated by `make docs` and is committed on purpose, so that
# the API reference can be read here without installing doxygen. It is the one
# thing this build produces that belongs in git.
